# gitbulk repo list — one GitHub slug per line.
#
# Format: owner/repo
#   - The exact slug GitHub uses in URLs (e.g. github.com/<owner>/<repo>)
#   - No protocol, no `.git` suffix, no local path
#
# Examples of VALID entries:
#   provenant-dev/origin-platform
#   dhh1128/gitbulk
#
# Examples of INVALID entries (will fail validation):
#   git@github.com:provenant-dev/origin-platform.git    (remote URL, not a slug)
#   https://github.com/provenant-dev/origin-platform    (URL, not a slug)
#   /home/daniel/code/origin-platform                   (filesystem path, not a slug)
#   provenant-dev/origin-platform.git                   (trailing .git not allowed)
#
# Local clone path: gitbulk assumes the local clone lives at
# `<code-root>/<repo-basename>`, where code-root defaults to `~/code/` and
# can be overridden per-invocation via `--code-root PATH`. Only subcommands
# that need a working tree (`dispatch`, `rebase-onto-default`) actually
# read the local clone; `report`, `merge`, `close-stale`, and `summarize`
# operate purely against the GitHub API.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Duplicate slugs are logged as WARNINGs and silently deduped (first wins).

# Provenant
provenant-dev/origin-platform
provenant-dev/origin-agent-svc
provenant-dev/origin-clerk-svc
provenant-dev/agentprep

# Open source
# hyperledger/aries-cloudagent-python
